            <ArticleTitle>Correlation of exercise induced hypotension and development of complications during treadmill stress test.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>519</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Exercise induced hypotension was observed in 41 of 354 patients studied. Fourteen of 41 as against 3 out of the remaining 313 developed complications, like atrial and ventricular arrhythmias, heart block, severe angina and left ventricular failure. Close monitoring of BP during exercise testing is mandatory.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
